										part of a fragmented element if there are three fragments,
										or the second fragment if there are four fragments</desc>
								</valItem>
								<valItem mode="change" ident="F">
									<desc versionDate="2024-09-30" xml:lang="en">this is the final
										part of a fragmented element if there are two or three
										fragments, or the second to last part if there are four
										fragments</desc>
								</valItem>
								<valItem mode="add" ident="F2">
									<desc versionDate="2024-09-30" xml:lang="en">only used if there
										are four fragments, in that case this is the final part of
										the fragmented element</desc>
								</valItem>
								<valItem mode="change" ident="N">
									<desc versionDate="2024-09-30" xml:lang="en">the element is not
										fragmented, or no claim is made as to its completeness; this
										option is equivalent to not having the part-attribute on the
										element</desc>
								</valItem>
								<valItem mode="delete" ident="Y"/>
							</valList>
						</attDef>
					</attList>
